# Python Style and Tooling

- Follow Google Python Style: 4 spaces, max 80–100 cols, snake_case, type hints for public APIs.
- Prefer meaningful names; avoid 1–2 char identifiers in production code.
- Keep functions small; extract helpers for complex logic.
- Use `ruff` for lint/format; keep imports sorted (`isort` style). Avoid unused imports.
- Use `pytest` fixtures and `@pytest.mark.parametrize` instead of loops/conditionals in tests.
- Avoid logic in tests (no-loop-in-tests). Move loops into fixtures or parametrize.
- Use `raise ... from e` when translating exceptions (see [exception-chaining.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/exception-chaining.mdc)).
- Don’t re-raise with `raise e`; use bare `raise` to preserve tracebacks.
